WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.354
Hi! You eat 1/5 of a cake, then 2/5 more. How much altogether? Today we'll add and subtract fractions with the same bottom number.

2
00:00:12.504 --> 00:00:19.218
1/5 plus 2/5: 1 part plus 2 parts is 3 parts, so 3/5.

3
00:00:19.368 --> 00:00:24.282
The size of each part doesn't change, so the bottom 5 stays the same.

4
00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:26.970
Add only the top numbers.

5
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:34.122
When the top and bottom are the same, it's one whole: 6/6 is 1.

6
00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:41.802
5/7 minus 2/7: 5 parts minus 2 parts leaves 3 parts, so 3/7.

7
00:00:41.952 --> 00:00:46.746
Subtraction is the same: keep the bottom, subtract the tops.

8
00:00:46.896 --> 00:00:55.602
1 minus 3/4: think of 1 as 4/4. Take away 3 parts and 1 part is left: 1/4.

9
00:00:55.752 --> 00:01:01.026
Draw a strip cut into equal parts and shade it to check.

10
00:01:01.176 --> 00:01:05.874
Watch out! Don't add 5 and 5 to get 10 on the bottom!

11
00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:10.386
Each part is still a fifth. There are just more parts.

12
00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:15.906
So 1/5 plus 2/5 is 3/5.

13
00:01:16.056 --> 00:01:24.642
Your turn! What is 3/8 plus 4/8? Pause and think.

14
00:01:24.792 --> 00:01:32.370
Keep the bottom: 3 plus 4 is 7, so 7/8. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:41.394
Another one! What is 6/9 minus 2/9? Pause and think.

16
00:01:41.544 --> 00:01:49.290
Keep the bottom: 6 minus 2 is 4, so 4/9. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:57.834
Here's another! What is 1 minus 2/5? Pause and think.

18
00:01:57.984 --> 00:02:06.210
Think of 1 as 5/5. 5 minus 2 is 3, so 3/5. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:17.874
Try one more! You ate 2/6 of a pizza, then 3/6 more. How much altogether? Pause and think.

20
00:02:18.024 --> 00:02:24.738
2 plus 3 is 5, so 5/6 altogether. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:24.888 --> 00:02:33.882
Try one more! After eating 5/6, how much is left? Pause and think.

22
00:02:34.032 --> 00:02:42.546
A whole is 6/6. Take away 5/6 and 1/6 is left. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:42.696 --> 00:02:51.306
Last one! What is three eighths plus four eighths? Pause and think.

24
00:02:51.456 --> 00:02:58.266
Keep the bottom, add 3 and 4: seven eighths. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:58.416 --> 00:03:07.890
Remember: with the same bottom number, keep the bottom and add or subtract the tops. 1 is the same as a fraction with equal top and bottom.

26
00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:14.154
Share a fruit with your family today and say what fraction you ate altogether!

